00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:07,499
I think I'll refrain from any more
goblin slaying for the time being.

262
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:13,440
I was way overconfident and got
into too many dangerous situations.

263
00:18:14,420 --> 00:18:19,960
I'll have to do a lot more training
before taking on the next challenge.

264
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:31,657
So it was a goblin emperor huh?

265
00:18:31,740 --> 00:18:37,297
It must have been quite powerful with
this size mana stone it's larger than

266
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:42,237
normal according to the reports it was
several times the size of a goblin king!

267
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:47,817
I'm sure it was the size
is unusual the magic

268
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:50,665
empire may be responsible
for the event itself?

269
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:53,200
But still, this stone, though...

270
00:18:54,040 --> 00:18:58,580
We think, sir, it could be a demon's
heart from the holy theocracy of Mithra.

271
00:18:59,040 --> 00:18:59,870
How is Lin?

272
00:19:00,220 --> 00:19:01,920
Only minor wounds.

273
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:05,040
It must have been a terribly hard battle.

274
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:07,937
It's amazing they were able to survive.

275
00:19:08,020 --> 00:19:10,977
The monster itself hid
behind a powerful seal

276
00:19:11,060 --> 00:19:13,620
and ambushed them in the Forest of Beasts.

277
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:17,005
The lady believes it had
been there a few days.

278
00:19:17,280 --> 00:19:19,657
And in fact, maybe even more than that.

279
00:19:19,740 --> 00:19:24,160
A few days, so this seal is one that
not even the secret core can perceive.

280
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:27,557
But how are they transporting such a bulky

281
00:19:27,640 --> 00:19:30,077
thing all the way here in the first place?

282
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:32,040
If they use summoning magic,

283
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:35,337
the sensory network in the
capital should have caught it.

284
00:19:35,420 --> 00:19:37,596
Did nothing show up in the perimeter?

285
00:19:37,860 --> 00:19:39,937
The number of goblins was decreasing,

286
00:19:40,020 --> 00:19:43,608
so the Adventurer's Guild
requested an investigation into it.

287
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:47,924
There may have been several similar
cases in other areas as well.

288
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:53,621
Well, this report is a summary of questionable
instances from the last three months.

289
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,235
Well done, gentlemen.

290
00:19:58,180 --> 00:19:59,709
Continue with the inquiry.

291
00:20:00,460 --> 00:20:01,600
Well, look at you.

292
00:20:01,840 --> 00:20:03,897
I never thought that the little runt from

293
00:20:03,980 --> 00:20:06,517
way back when would
grow up to slay goblins.

294
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:09,317
It was so much nastier
than I thought it would be.

295
00:20:09,400 --> 00:20:14,177
But Lin came in at the last moment, and
we managed to get the job done no problem.

296
00:20:14,260 --> 00:20:16,240
Oh no, that's not how it went.

297
00:20:19,660 --> 00:20:20,490
It happened.

298
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:21,880
My very first hunt.

299
00:20:22,040 --> 00:20:23,117
I should celebrate.

300
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:27,557
It may be just another quest to other
adventurers, but to me, this is, you know,

301
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:28,470
everything.

302
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:29,720
You did well.

303
00:20:30,780 --> 00:20:34,057
Best to just watch from the
sidelines and let her handle it.

304
00:20:34,140 --> 00:20:38,120
And I guess probably it's the wiser
choice, too, eh? You know what?

305
00:20:38,580 --> 00:20:41,397
I'm just grateful I got to
help her out a little bit.

306
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:44,620
I have no idea where I'd be
if Lin hadn't been there.

307
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:48,240
But I'm the one that just
helped you out, remember?

308
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:52,660
Well, even goblins can still be a
threat to newbies from time to time.

309
00:20:53,180 --> 00:20:55,768
But it was a good
experience for you, right?

310
00:20:56,180 --> 00:20:57,709
Exactly, it certainly was.

311
00:20:57,880 --> 00:21:02,277
Until I saw one in real life, I had no
idea goblins were anything like that.

312
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:05,497
And who knew about the stone on
its forehead being a weak point?

313
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:06,992
A stone on the forehead?

314
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:08,457
What are you talking about?

315
00:21:08,540 --> 00:21:10,597
Yeah, kind of a shiny reddish color.

316
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:12,386
And kind of pretty, actually.

317
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:15,140
Oh, you mean a monostone.

318
00:21:15,280 --> 00:21:18,104
It's normally buried in
the heart or the throat.

319
00:21:18,900 --> 00:21:19,730
Hmm.

320
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:22,666
Are you sure that was
really a goblin, my boy?

321
00:21:23,120 --> 00:21:24,237
Yeah, well, of course.

322
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:26,060
A goblin, right? Indeed.

323
00:21:26,420 --> 00:21:29,297
If that's what you say it is,
instructor, then that is that.

324
00:21:29,380 --> 00:21:31,440
No matter what anybody says. Hmm.

325
00:21:32,200 --> 00:21:34,376
Might have been a rare type, I guess.

326
00:21:35,900 --> 00:21:38,429
All right, let's see
the proof of the kill.

327
00:21:39,020 --> 00:21:40,608
I'm going to get your cash.

328
00:21:42,940 --> 00:21:46,500
the right ear i told you
to bring back the right ear

329
00:21:51,360 --> 00:21:52,520
no way

330
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:59,340
um we might have set that
goblin on fire you did what

331
00:22:24,640 --> 00:22:31,640
are

332
00:22:32,980 --> 00:22:37,540
you doing?

333
00:23:36,600 --> 00:23:39,180
We'll be back.
